This parameter is required.', example='lb-5snthcyu1x10g7tywj7iu****'),
  requestTimeout?: int32(name='RequestTimeout', description='The request timeout period. Default value: 60. Valid values: **1** to **180**. Unit: seconds.
> If a backend server does not send a response within the timeout period, load balancing stops waiting and returns an HTTP 504 error code to the client.', example='60'),
  scheduler?: string(name='Scheduler', description='The scheduling algorithm. Valid values:
- **wrr**: Backend servers with higher weights receive more requests.
- **wlc**: Requests are distributed based on the weights and actual loads (connections) of backend servers. If the weights are the same, backend servers with fewer connections receive more requests.
- **rr**: Requests are evenly distributed to backend servers in sequence.
- **sch**: Consistent hashing based on source IP addresses. Requests from the same source IP address are distributed to the same backend server.
- **qch**: Consistent hashing based on QUIC Connection IDs. Requests with the same QUIC Connection ID are distributed to the same backend server.
- **iqch**: Consistent hashing based on specific three bytes of the iQUIC CID. Requests with the same 2nd to 4th bytes are distributed to the same backend server.', example='wrr'),
  serverCertificateId?: string(name='ServerCertificateId', description='The ID of the server certificate.', example='6027667'),
  unhealthyThreshold?: int32(name='UnhealthyThreshold', description='The number of consecutive failed health checks that must occur before the health check status of a backend server changes from success (reachable) to fail (unreachable). Valid values: **2** to **10**.
> This parameter takes effect only when HealthCheck is set to on.', example='3'),
}

